cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Before we go further, let me discuss West's bidding. Apparently, West with 8 HCP + 1 length point + 1 quality suit point + 1 for doubleton = 11, assumed the hand is strong enough to make a forcing 3-card limit raise--1N instead of 1@S.|
PG| ***** 2 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|On the other hand, 1N bid definitely denies 4 spades while West has five spades. Systemically, 1@S is the correct bid and is also forcing. Having said that, as you will see they will end up in 4@H regardless.|
PG| ***** 3 ***** |


