UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Well played by East. Ducking the spade probably doesn't cost anything because even if it loses to the @SK, it sets up a club discard. |
PG| ***** 16 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|However, it turns out, at trick two had North led back a club, which is a better defense, then the hand would go down because we would take 1 spade, 1 club, and 2 hearts. Given East bid 3@D, a club return is likely to be better than a diamond return.|
PG| ***** 17 ***** |


