mb|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Most players play ^*BSystems on, Stolen Bid Doubles^*n after interference over 1N. If you play that, the double is "stolen bid" meaning East was intending to bid 2@D as a heart transfer. Many other players play a system called |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lebensohl,Lebensohl^*N|CP||FP||at|. |

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 43 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In that case double is takeout. Suits at the 2 level are to play and 2N is a special conventional bid which is too complicated to explain here. I suggest you play systems on because |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lebensohl,Lebensohl^*N|CP||FP||at| can be quite complicated. |
PG| ***** 44 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So since we don't play |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lebensohl,Lebensohl^*N|CP||FP||at| at this table, I think East has to bid |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=Stayman,The Stayman ^*N|CP||FP||at| by bidding 3@D and hoping partner has a 4-card major or enough HCP to make 3N. Certainly, it is possible since East has 9 HCP.|
PG| ***** 45 ***** |


mb|3D|mb|P|mb|3S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|4S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree with 4@S. There is much upside and little downside and to be consistent, 3@D commits their side to game when West has no 4-card major and bids 3NT over 3@D. So might as well bid game when they have a major. It might go down but that is why the opponents interfere.|
PG| ***** 46 ***** |


