UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|One small defensive error worth noting. 2nd hand low is usually right and certainly right on this hand when I played a club at trick three. Think about it. If I have the @CK, the @CA is still taking a trick and if partner has the @CK ducking the @CA is fine. By taking the @CA allowed me to set up a club trick.|
PG| ***** 107 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|As to 2@S call by West. It is nice to preempt aggressively at favorable vulnerability (you not vulnerable, they are vulnerable). However, I disagree with 2@S on this particular hand. West has only a 5-card suit and a balanced hand with no shortness.|
PG| ***** 108 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Sometimes you will make a jump overcall with a 5-card suit when you are short in the opponents' suit. But on this hand that is not the case plus West has a pretty decent hand. So I think 1@S is better although 2@S did give North a problem as preempts often do.

|
PG| ***** 109 ***** |


